"""Walk-through of lesson 28, Monolith vs Microservices.

Example numbers (mine, checked by script): 50 engineers in 6 teams. A monolith releases once a week (everyone waits for everyone).
Six teams that each ship 3 times a week = 18 deploys a week once the app is split. Every part is up 99.9% of the time:
availability of a page that needs n parts = 0.999^n: 1 part 99.9% (8.8 h a year); 3 parts 99.7%; 5 parts 99.5% (about 44 h a year).
A network call is shown as about 2 ms. A local read copy lags about 1 second behind the owner's data.
"""
